---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import headshot from "../assets/headshots/headshot-1.jpg";

const honors = [
  "Kofi Annan Scholar",
  "Dean's List",
  "Fleming First-Generation Scholar",
  "Full-Ride Scholarship",
];
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  description="About Makol J. Chuol: from Kakuma Refugee Camp to Macalester College, and why engineering and community work come from the same place."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 pt-14 pb-16 sm:px-8 sm:pt-20">
    <div class="grid gap-10 sm:grid-cols-[auto_1fr] sm:items-start sm:gap-14">
      <Image
        src={headshot}
        alt="Portrait of Makol J. Chuol"
        width={280}
        height={340}
        class="h-56 w-44 rounded-2xl object-cover shadow-sm sm:h-72 sm:w-56"
        data-reveal
      />

      <div data-reveal>
        <p class="text-sm font-medium tracking-wide text-accent uppercase">
          About
        </p>
        <h1 class="mt-3 font-serif text-3xl text-ink sm:text-4xl">
          Two threads, one way of working.
        </h1>

        <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          I'm a builder first. Give me a system I don't understand, whether
          it's a codebase, a curriculum, or a classroom, and I'll spend more
          time reading it than touching it, because the fix that actually
          holds is never obvious until the read is done. Curiosity is the
          real skill. Code, mentorship, and training programs are just where
          it shows up.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          I'm a senior at Macalester College studying computer science,
          graduating May 2027. My path into tech ran sideways before it ran
          straight: years teaching in Kakuma, Kenya taught me to build things
          people actually need before I learned to build things that simply
          work. Elimisha Kakuma, a program founded by former refugees who'd
          studied in the U.S., is what eventually opened the door to
          Macalester itself.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          Outside of work, I write. My grandmother's stories, the ones
          where she taught me to read the stars for weather and warning,
          are where I first learned to pay attention. Those lessons taught
          me patience and curiosity long before any classroom did, and
          that instinct still shapes how I build.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          I publish some of it on{" "}
          <a
            href="https://mjc412.substack.com"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="text-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-accent"
            >Substack</a
          >, under mjc@412.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 py-10 sm:px-8">
    <div class="border-t border-line pt-10" data-reveal>
      <h2 class="font-serif text-lg text-ink">Education</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-base text-ink-soft">
        Macalester College: B.A. Computer Science, minor in Educational
        Studies. Expected May 2027.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
        {
          honors.map((h) => (
            <span class="rounded-full border border-line px-3 py-1 text-xs text-ink-soft">
              {h}
            </span>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 pt-4 pb-16 sm:px-8">
    <div class="border-t border-line pt-10" data-reveal>
      <p class="font-serif text-xl leading-relaxed text-ink-soft italic sm:text-2xl">
        &ldquo;Peace is not something we deliver from outside a community;
        it's something we help a community recognize it already knows how
        to build.&rdquo;
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
